<div class="mk-crumbbar"><div class="mk-wrap in"><a href="#">Markets</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/markets/industrial-iot">Industrial &amp; IoT</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><span class="here">RFID Asset Tracking</span></div></div><div class="mk-spoke-grid"><aside class="mk-side"><div class="side-head"><span class="side-head-label">Industrial &amp; IoT products</span><button type="button" class="mk-side-toggle" aria-label="Collapse sidebar"><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></span></button></div><a class="s" href="/markets/industrial-iot/pcba-box-build"><span class="abbr">PB</span><span class="label">PCBA &amp; Box Build</span></a><a class="s" href="/markets/industrial-iot/iot-device-assembly"><span class="abbr">ID</span><span class="label">IoT Device Assembly</span></a><a class="s active" href="/markets/industrial-iot/rfid-asset-tracking"><span class="abbr">RT</span><span class="label">RFID Asset Tracking</span></a><div class="helper"><div class="h">Not sure which fits?</div><p>Tell us what the product does and where it runs and we&rsquo;ll point you to the right line.</p><a class="cta" href="/contact">Work with us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></aside><div class="mk-spoke-main"><section class="mk-hero" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="light" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap mk-hero-in"><div><div class="mk-eyebrow">Industrial &amp; IoT &middot; RFID Asset Tracking</div><h1 class="mk-h1">RFID tags for industrial &amp; retail asset tracking</h1><p class="mk-lede">Industrial RFID tags can require ruggedized construction, reliable performance on metal and resistance to handling, cleaning and outdoor exposure. Hana manufactures UHF tags and inlays for these environments, with constructions selected according to the mounting surface and application requirements.</p><div class="mk-btns"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-primary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Talk to us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a><a href="#specialize-rfid-asset-tracking" class="hana-btn hana-btn-secondary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">What we specialize in</a></div></div><div class="mk-hero-media"><div class="mk-ph" style="aspect-ratio:auto;height:420px;border-bottom:0;"><img src="~/images/photos/mk-industrial-iot-card-rfid-asset-tag.webp" alt="Industrial UHF RFID asset tags" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block;"/></div></div></div></section><section id="specialize-rfid-asset-tracking" data-hana-bg="hex" data-variant="light" data-fade="none" style="background:var(--bg);border-top:1px solid var(--line);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="mk-wrap" style="position:relative;z-index:1;padding-top:64px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 class="mk-h2">What we specialize in</h2><p class="mk-body">Hana manufactures hardened, rubber-embeddable and on-metal UHF tag constructions, together with temperature-sensing formats where required. Inlays and straps are produced on automated roll-to-roll manufacturing lines, including six lines at Hana's Jiaxing facility. Hana has more than 20 years of RFID design and manufacturing experience.</p></div><div class="mk-sheet"><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">Rugged and on-metal UHF tags</span></div><div class="desc">Hardened tag constructions for equipment and metal surfaces, with the format selected according to the mounting surface and operating environment.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">UHF inlays and straps</span></div><div class="desc">Inlays and straps produced on automated roll-to-roll manufacturing lines.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">Rubber-embeddable and temperature-sensing formats</span></div><div class="desc">Embeddable constructions and temperature-sensing tags available where required by the application.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">04</span><span class="t">Encoding, unique ID and read verification</span></div><div class="desc">Unique identification and read-performance verification applied to the finished tag as part of the manufacturing process.</div></div></div><div class="mk-caplinks"><p class="note">See RFID Inlay for the antenna, converting and tuning processes supporting these tag constructions.</p><div class="links"><a href="/capabilities/rfid-smart-tags/rfid-inlays">Explore RFID Inlay <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></div></div></section><section class="mk-dark"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div style="max-width:820px;"><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark">Ruggedization and read range</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="margin:0 0 14px;">Industrial tag performance depends on both mechanical construction and RF performance after installation. Materials, encapsulation, antenna design and the spacing required for on-metal operation are selected according to the mounting surface and operating environment. Read performance can then be verified on the completed tag. Hana's UHF tags are certified under the ARC (Auburn) program in the USA and China, providing independent verification of tag performance.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:56px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:24px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">Footprint</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Where we build</h2></div><div class="mk-locs"><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/jiaxing"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">China</span></span><div class="nm">Jiaxing</div><div class="note">automated RFID inlay lines</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/ohio"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">USA</span></span><div class="nm">Ohio</div><div class="note">UHF inlays, straps and ruggedized tags</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a></div><p style="margin:18px 0 0;"><a href="/locations" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;">All locations <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></a></p></div></section><section style="background:#fff;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:22px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">FAQ</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="max-width:860px;"><details class="mk-faq" open><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What makes an industrial RFID tag different from a label?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Industrial RFID tags use a built construction designed for the mounting surface and operating environment. This can include encapsulation, ruggedized materials and on-metal antenna designs that allow a UHF tag to remain readable when mounted against metal.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What read range can industrial UHF tags achieve?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Read range depends on tag construction, mounting surface and reader configuration, so it is established per program rather than quoted as a single figure. Hana can verify read performance on the finished tag, and its UHF tags are certified under the ARC (Auburn) program in the USA and China.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">Does Hana have experience manufacturing RFID at volume?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Yes. Hana has more than 20 years of RFID design and manufacturing experience, supported by automated roll-to-roll inlay lines, including six lines at Jiaxing, with inlay and strap production also running in Ohio.</p></details></div><div style="margin-top:40px;padding-top:26px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><a href="/markets/industrial-iot" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;"><i data-lucide="arrow-left" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Back to the Industrial &amp; IoT market hub</a></div></div></section><section class="mk-cta" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="dark" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark" style="max-width:520px;">Talk to us about your asset-tracking program</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="font-size:16px;max-width:480px;">Tell us what you need built and we will come back with a plan.</p></div><div class="acts"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-on-dark" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Contact us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a></div></div></section></div></div>